{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 9, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**Discovering Japan: A Whirlwind Adventure**\n\nLast summer, I traded my usual routine for the neon lights and serene temples of Japan. My journey began in Tokyo, where the hum of the Shinkansen (bullet train) whisked me into a world of futuristic energy. The city’s skyline blended steel and glass with traditional lanterns, while Shibuya Crossing left me breathless with its bustling crowds. A visit to Akihabara revealed a haven for tech and anime lovers, and a late-night ramen feast at Ichiran kept me up half the night.\n\nFrom Tokyo, I took the train to Kyoto, where time seemed to slow. Wandering through Arashiyama’s bamboo forest felt like stepping into a painting, and the golden gates of Kinkaku-ji shimmered under the sun. A tea ceremony at a quiet ryokan taught me patience, while the street food at Nishiki Market—tasty takoyaki and matcha soft serve—kept me happily full.\n\nMy last stop was Osaka, the city of laughter. Dotonbori’s giant crab sign and glowing street food stalls were pure magic. I tried my first okonomiyaki (savory pancake) at a local spot and laughed as my attempt went comically wrong. A day trip to Nara left me surrounded by deer that bowed for crackers, and the towering Todai-ji temple felt awe-inspiring.\n\nJapan was a masterclass in contrast—high-tech and historic, loud and peaceful. Every bite, view, and interaction felt like a new discovery. Even now, the sounds of distant temple bells and the aroma of fresh sushi linger in my memory. If you ever hesitate, just go—Japan doesn’t just happen; it *haunts* your dreams afterward.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.07108993083238602}, {"token": "Dis", "logprob": -2.5123181343078613}, {"token": "cover", "logprob": -0.00011145447206217796}, {"token": "ing", "logprob": -0.0006305375136435032}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.3966290056705475}, {"token": ":", "log